    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a high-upside slate today, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez**, who leads the team with an elite 82.97 score against Melton. His matchup is optimized by a favorable SP xERA of 4.62 and a projected #2 spot in the order, pairing perfectly with his 0.449 xwOBA. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-focused strategy today with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (75.59), who remains a must-start despite the tough matchup against Freddy Peralta; his projected leadoff spot and a 92% stolen base success rate against the starter\u2019s slow delivery make him an essential engine for our SB category. **Junior Caminero** (70.81) and **Trea Turner** (66.52) also provide significant ceiling, with the latter benefiting from a +10% order bonus that keeps him in high-priority territory despite a respectable 3.95 xERA from the opposition.\n\nPlatoon advantages play a massive role in today\u2019s optimization, specifically for **Lars Nootbaar** (60.52) and **Colt Keith** (61.75). **Lars Nootbaar** is enjoying a +11% dynamic platoon bump against Zac Gallen, which pushes his value well above his base projection. Meanwhile, **Carson Benge** was our most difficult bench decision, falling just short at 39.99. While his projected leadoff spot provided a +10% boost, the optimizer favored the higher overall efficiency of our starting OF/Utility slots, ultimately capping **Carson Benge** due to a harsh -15% drag from Matthew Boyd\u2019s skill profile and a disadvantageous L/L platoon matchup. We will continue to monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Yordan Alvarez** closely, as any shift away from their projected slots could necessitate a recalibration of our expected production.",
